<title>EGYPT: Egypt police arrest seven striking workers.</title>
<headline>Egypt police arrest seven striking workers.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egyptian police said on Thursday they had arrested seven striking public transport workers in the Delta province of Gharbiya.</p>
<p>Strikes are illegal in Egypt.</p>
<p>Some 2,700 bus conductors, drivers and other transport workers in the provincial capital Tanta have been on strike since Wednesday to protest against the cancellation of their annual bonuses.</p>
<p>The seven workers were on their way to the nearby el-Mahalla el-Kobra town, where 200 of their colleagues had returned to work on Thursday after a one-day strike, police said.</p>
</text>
